ntdll: M_PERTURB is not in bionic.

Proton calls `mallopt( M_PERTURB, 0xff )` on the way into ntdll's start-up and
`mallopt( M_PERTURB, 0 )` on the way out, so that a use-after-free of an
allocation made during loader init reads 0xff rather than plausible data. It is
Valve's addition -- upstream Wine 11.14 has no reference to M_PERTURB anywhere.

M_PERTURB is a glibc constant. Bionic's malloc.h defines M_DECAY_TIME and
nothing else of that family, so both calls fail to compile:

    dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c:2483: error: use of undeclared identifier 'M_PERTURB'
    dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c:2492: error: use of undeclared identifier 'M_PERTURB'

Compiled out rather than emulated. Android's allocator has no equivalent knob,
and passing a constant bionic does not define would be a no-op with a magic
number in it. Nothing in the function reads the setting back, so removing it
costs only the hardening it provides -- which glibc builds keep, because the
guard is on the macro rather than on __ANDROID__.
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
index 3f883a9c41..adba5b12da 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
@@ -2480,7 +2480,22 @@ static void start_main_thread(void)
     set_thread_teb( teb );
 #endif
 
+    /* VESSEL: bionic's mallopt() has no M_PERTURB.
+     *
+     * Proton fills freshly freed memory with 0xff across ntdll's own start-up
+     * and turns it off again once the loader is up, so that a use-after-free of
+     * an early allocation is loud instead of a silent read of plausible data.
+     * It is a hardening measure, not a dependency: the identifier is glibc's,
+     * bionic's malloc.h defines only M_DECAY_TIME, and nothing in this function
+     * observes the setting.
+     *
+     * Compiled out rather than replaced. Android's allocator offers no
+     * equivalent, and calling mallopt() with a glibc constant it does not know
+     * would be a silently ignored no-op with a number in it.
+     */
+#ifdef M_PERTURB
     mallopt( M_PERTURB, 0xff );
+#endif
     init_startup_info();
     *(ULONG_PTR *)&peb->CloudFileFlags = get_image_address();
     set_load_order_app_name( main_wargv[0] );
@@ -2489,7 +2504,9 @@ static void start_main_thread(void)
     load_ntdll();
     load_wow64_ntdll( main_image_info.Machine );
     load_apiset_dll();
+#ifdef M_PERTURB
     mallopt( M_PERTURB, 0 );
+#endif
     server_init_process_done();
 }
 
